  "_comment": "Negative. The 2026 comparison cites a machine-adjudication proof that names the 2019 comparison in rkaf:proofComparisonContext: a stale pass, replayed to back a fresh discrepancy. The proof record itself is untouched, so rkaf:proofRecordDigest is no help -- it is the CITATION that is fraudulent. Caught by the PRE-EXISTING rkaf:ResolverProofComparisonBindingShape (spec/rkaf-analysis.md 4.3), which applies to a machine-adjudication proof for the plainest possible reason: it always was a plain rkaf:ResolverProofRecord, never a second type carved out for its own citation rules. (This fixture also, incidentally, trips rkaf:MachineAdjudicationIndependentPairShape on both comparisons, since each cites only the one proof -- a single machine-adjudication proof can never form a pair regardless of the citation defect above; that shape is exercised in isolation by the other negative fixtures in this directory.)"
